.th ENTAB I 13/7/79
.sh  NAME
entab \*- replace blanks with tabs where possible
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd entab
[ infile [ outfile ] ]
.sh DESCRIPTION
Entab where possible replaces strings of blanks by tab character (and blanks).
If no output file is specified standard output is used.
If no input file is specified standard input (and standard output) is used.
A single blank is never replaced by a tab.
.sh "SEE ALSO"
detab (I)
.sh BUGS
